After my first excursion into the game and finding that I was dead of 
starvation within 10 minutes (real time), I figure that I need to get a 
better handle on how time works in this game.  For instance, I get that 
moving one space is considered a "turn," but how long is that exactly?  And 
what other actions/commands take a "turn" to complete?  Which don't take any 
time at all?  Are there any that take some fraction of a turn?

This seems like it would be important to know.
- If I'm standing near some monster and decide to (s)earch for hidden 
doors/traps am I giving that monster enough time to pounce on me?  How about 
if I just take a good look at him with the "/" key?  Or what if I put on 
that helmet I found in the other room?

- If I've been though the level and can't find the stairs to the next level 
(why I died the on the first level), I know that what I need to do is 
(s)earch for a hidden door or passage I missed.  I see two ways to do this: 
1. Step-n10s to search each space 10 times before moving on to the next 
space or 2. Step-s to search each space once before giving the whole area a 
second sweep.  Which would be more efficient game-time-wise? 




